Return Value
The method does not have a return value.
It outputs error messages, which might cause the method to fail, because:
• The specified Worker is a class object.
• The specified Worker is brokered automatically.
• The specified Worker cannot transport parts.
• The specified Worker already carries a part.
• The number of parts to be carried is greater than the current Capacity of the Worker.
• The part does not exist or does not have the correct object type.
• The Destination does not exist or does not have the correct object type.
• You did not specify a Destination and the part/the parts do not have a Destination of their own.
• The part itself, that is to be transported, has a defined Destination, which differs from the specified
Destination.
• The parts to be transported have to be picked up at different locations.
• The part or one of the parts is already being transported by a Worker.
• No parts are to be picked up and carried away at the Station by the Worker.
• An error occurred while sending the Worker for picking up or transporting the parts.
Examples
waituntil .Resources.Worker:1.HasOrder = false
.Resources.Worker:1.transportPart(Station.cont, Station1)
SimTalk
cancelTransportPart [SimTalk]
Destination [SimTalk] - MUs
Read-Only Attributes of the Worker
_Read-Only Attributes of the Worker
The Worker provides:
• The read-only attributes listed in the table of contents to the left.
• All read-only attributes of the Exporter, as the Worker is an Exporter with the capacity of 1.
Read-Only Attributes of the Worker
11-3214 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The _Read-Only Attributes of All Objects.
You can query the values of the read-only attributes, but you cannot set them as Plant Simulation
computes the value for the point-in-time at which you query it. In most cases a read-only attribute
corresponds to an unavailable dialog item on one of the tabs of the object, for example on the tab
Statistics.
To view all of the methods, read-only attributes, and attributes of the object, open the window Show
Attributes and Methods. The figure below illustrates the information using the example of the object
Station.
• Select Show Attributes and Methods on the context menu of the Class Library to show the methods,
read-only attributes, and attributes of the selected Class [general description].
• Press the F8 key or click Show Attributes and Methods on the Home ribbon tab of the Frame into
which you inserted an instance to show the methods, read-only attributes, and attributes of the
selected Instance [general description].
To query the value of a read-only attribute, you might, for example, type:
print .Resources.Worker:1.StatTraveledDistance
